      "updated_at": "2026-08-18T11:23:49Z",
      "body": "@sestnastka This is now implemented in v2 and ready to try in the beta.\n\nPR #6609 has been merged into `release/v2`: https://github.com/homarr-labs/homarr/pull/6609\n\nYou can find the v2 beta image and demo in the pinned testing issue: https://github.com/homarr-labs/homarr/issues/6600\n\nIt adds named Docker/Podman endpoints through `DOCKER_ENDPOINTS`. Each endpoint can use a socket, TLS, or explicitly acknowledged insecure TCP transport. Containers stay scoped to their endpoint, so actions such as logs, start, stop, restart, and remove are sent to the correct Docker host. If one host is unavailable, Homarr keeps showing the healthy hosts and reports the unavailable one separately. The existing `DOCKER_HOSTNAMES` / `DOCKER_PORTS` setup remains supported.\n\nUpdated v2 documentation:\n- Docker integration: https://github.com/homarr-labs/homarr/blob/release/v2/apps/docs/docs/integrations/docker/index.mdx\n- Environment variables: https://github.com/homarr-labs/homarr/blob/release/v2/apps/docs/docs/advanced/environment-variables/index.mdx\n\nOne limitation: endpoints are configured server-side through environment variables; they are not yet added dynamically from the GUI. Your two-host setup should be a good beta test case\u2014please let us know how it behaves.",
